From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 07:40:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: restrict libservo_arkweb.so exported symbols
 and load it with RTLD_LOCAL

Hide the dependency/std C symbols (ICU4X, encoding_rs, brotli, aws-lc,
cxx runtime, ...) that leaked into the dynamic symbol table via
--exclude-libs,ALL, and add a version script declaring the two dlsym'd
factory symbols as the public ABI. Cuts exported dynsyms 641 -> 29.

The OHOS loader patch now dlopens the shim with RTLD_LOCAL instead of
RTLD_GLOBAL. The shim is self-contained and its two factory symbols are
resolved via dlsym on the returned handle, so RTLD_GLOBAL only served to
leak the shim's symbols into the app's global scope. Verified on the rk3568:
the shim still loads and renders a data: page (no dlopen failure under
RTLD_NOW).

Rebase ohos-patches/0001 onto OpenHarmony-v7.0-Release (web_webview
12cb9a37bbba) to match the re-synced NWeb headers. Only the context and
line numbers change; the patch content is the same. It targets this
patch because this is the last one in the stack that edits 0001.

Validation: Test by checking llvm-nm -D --defined-only on libservo_arkweb.so (only the intended exports remain), then launching the test app (the shim dlopens the engine) and running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_render.py. Rebase of ohos-patches/0001 onto OpenHarmony-v7.0-Release: Built a full rk3568 arm64 image from OpenHarmony-v7.0-Release with ohos-patches/0001 and 0002 applied (without 0002 it boot-loops on appspawn) and flashed a HiHope DAYU200 (OpenHarmony 7.0, API 26); `./mach build --ohos --release --no-package -p arkweb`, deployed with `tools/deploy.py`, test app installed with `tools/build_test_app.py`; `HDC_TARGET=<serial> uv run --with pytest --with hdc-py --with pillow python -m pytest ports/arkweb/tools`: 35 passed, 1 xfailed. `tools/gen_stubs.py --check` is clean.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-10-09 restack -- folded in "ports/arkweb: dlopen the shim with RTLD_LOCAL in the OHOS loader")
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; patch rebase and on-device testing)
